# Per-module pytest logs and reports are CI artifacts, not research evidence.
test-results/

# The v2 selection result stream is a projection of the verified shards under
# research/shards_v2 and is regenerated from them (residual limitation RL2 of
# configs/research_v2_selection_authorization_1.json). At the size of the
# authorized run it exceeds the per-file push limit, so it is not committed.
research/results_v2.jsonl

# The v3 selection result stream is a projection of the verified shards under
# research/shards_v3 and is regenerated from them (residual limitation RL2 of
# configs/research_v3_selection_authorization_1.json). At the size of the
# authorized run it exceeds the per-file push limit, so it is not committed.
research/results_v3.jsonl

# The v4 selection result stream is a projection of the verified shards under
# research/shards_v4 and is regenerated from them (residual limitation RL2 of
# configs/research_v4_selection_authorization_1.json). At the size of the
# authorized run it exceeds the per-file push limit, so it is not committed.
research/results_v4.jsonl

# The v5 selection result stream is a projection of the verified shards under
# research/shards_v5 and is regenerated from them, for the same reason as the
# v2, the v3 and the v4 streams: at the size of the authorized run it exceeds
# the per-file push limit, so it is not committed. A v5 verifier treats its
# absence as "not materialized" and reports the shard projection's digest
# instead of failing (the v5 specification's result_stream_durability).
research/results_v5.jsonl
